  "notes": [
    "06 s8.4: prices live in a versioned model_prices table; a report pins the version it used. This file IS that table for intel; app/pricing stamps '<version>@sha256:<sha256 of this file's bytes>' on every ModelPrice it hands out.",
    "effective_from is the retrieval date: no vendor page states an effective date. Anthropic's page notes Sonnet 5's $2/$10 is now the standard price (the scheduled 2026-09-01 increase did not occur).",
    "cache_write is the vendor's per-token price for writing a prompt cache. Anthropic: the 5-minute cache write ($1.25x input); the ledger carries one cache-creation token class, so 1-hour writes (2x input) are under-priced by this table. OpenAI GPT-5.5 and earlier: 'No additional cache-write charge' (prompt-caching guide), so cache_write equals input; GPT-5.6 and later carry the page's explicit cache-write column. Google: the Gemini pricing page publishes a context-caching (read) price and an hourly storage price but no per-token cache-write price, so cache_write is null and app/pricing refuses to price those models rather than infer a number.",
    "A null in any of input/output/cache_write/cache_read makes the row unpinned: it stays here for the record and price_for() refuses it by name.",
    "Omitted on purpose (not invented): retired Anthropic models (Opus 4.1, Opus 4, Sonnet 4, Haiku 3.5) and Mythos (limited availability); OpenAI -pro models (no cached-input price on the page) and pre-GPT-4.1 legacy rows; Gemini models with prompt-size-tiered prices (gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-3.1-pro-preview) or time-limited prices (gemini-3.8/3.7/3.6-flash through 2026-12-31), image/audio/video/tts/embedding models."
  ],
